## window.api migration — what moved, what stays
**Moved** (post-init persist writes; routers already existed): `useGitDiffCollapse` task.update; `useContextManagerStore` + `useTabStore` settings.set.

**Stays on `window.api` by design** (not migratable / would regress): bootstrap reads that run before the tRPC client exists (`theme-init`, `useTabStore` init read, `main.tsx` boot error handler, `app.getTrpcPort`/`bootMark`/`isPlaywright`, `panels.getWindowId`); native ops (`files.getDropPaths/getPastePaths`, `warm.setProjectTabCounts` — no tRPC procedure); documented listeners (`theme.onChange`, `pty.on*`, `fs.onFileChanged`, `git.onCreateWorktreePhase`, `browser.*` native view ops); and `diagnostics.export` (the tRPC `exportBundle` is an intentionally-deferred UX change — native save dialog → browser download — per its own code comment). Zero-window.api in the renderer is therefore **not** fully reachable; the remainder is an irreducible bootstrap/native/listener set.

